# NerfHack fuzzing rcfile
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# A minimal, neutral config for automated fuzzing sessions
# (sys/unix/nerfhack-rr-fuzz.sh), deliberately independent of any player's
# personal $HOME/.nerfhackrc. Keeping fuzzing runs on a clean, close-to-default
# config means bugs found are representative of ordinary play, not artifacts
# of one player's MSGTYPE/menucolor/keybind customizations.
#
# Wired in automatically via NERFHACKOPTIONS=<path to this file> -- see
# nerfhack-rr-fuzz.sh. Not meant to be copied to $HOME; edit this file
# directly to change what fuzzing sessions run with.

# Fuzzer deaths are frequent and disposable; don't let them pollute the
# shared bones-file pool that real games draw from.
OPTIONS=!bones

# Skip per-turn checkpoint-file I/O. It exists for crash recovery, but every
# fuzzing session already runs under `rr record`, a far more complete safety
# net -- checkpointing here is just overhead that slows down turn throughput.
OPTIONS=!checkpoint
